  "evidence": [
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Parallel light bench rows cover the entire deck, with aisles cutting across them. A darker central seat block and elongated box lie at mid-length. Deck colour sampled at local (174,1270)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "Regional 2 m grid, heights above local ground. Median 7.4 m, P90 11.86 m, maximum 17.1 m. Cross sections rise east to west from roughly 2 to 13 m, peaking at 17 m over the central press box."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "Western Facilities stadium panorama shows two uncovered raked stands, open steel framing below the decks and the larger west bank.",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/fm/img/what_we_do/bldg/WAS.jpg"
    },
    {
      "kind": "osm",
      "note": "Footprint tagged building=grandstand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "Western Athletics describes the spectator stands and media press box.",
      "url": "https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/2010/6/9/Facilities_0609105641.aspx"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Each clipped tier approximates one row of the open seating rake. Aisle breaks, handrails, diagonal frame bracing and individual seats need dedicated grandstand geometry. Frame 138541239 points toward the stand from beyond London Hall, which blocks the line of sight. The 1 m lidar grid places the main press box along the rear edge between approximately z 1241 and 1264. There is a separate narrower box to the north. Along the north access the surface rises eastward from 0.5 m at x 194 to 3.2 m at x 198 near z 1204. The orthophoto does not resolve individual treads. The seating has no overhead canopy in the public stadium panorama. The dark patch is reserved seating. Hardstanding extends under the framing.",
